      en: "The Coast Watchers Memorial on Tarawa honors the civilian and military coast watchers who provided Allied forces with intelligence on Japanese movements during World War II. Erected in 1992 near the former US base on Betio, the monument features a stone stele with a metal plaque. Coast watchers, often locals or European planters, operated behind enemy lines at great personal risk. Their reports were vital to Allied successes in the Pacific. The memorial recognizes their bravery and sacrifice.",
